# Authority parent device CPU attribution

This finite nonproduct comparison isolates parent-device projection in the
complete leaf validator. It preserves before-read predicates, all four fresh
observations, conditional read order, descriptor lifetimes and original windows.
See the frozen [protocol](protocol.json) and
[result with evidence](../../docs/testing/performance/0.74/authority-parent-cost-result-20261025.md).

Eight independent processes per phase compare marker and record payloads using
balanced reference, identical-reference control, actual runtime and prototype
arms. Baseline runtime must calibrate against reference; integrated runtime must
calibrate against prototype. Both candidate upper CPU intervals must be at most
0.98. A successful libtest exit alone is neither that gate nor start admission.

```text
python tools/authority-parent-cost-074/test_review.py
```

`review.py::review(cohorts, phase)` consumes eight untouched stdout byte streams
and `prototype` or `installed`. Changed payloads, work, observation count, order,
types, flags or clocks refuse. It reuses only estimator/parser helpers from the
frozen directory reader. Synthetic reader controls are not benchmark results.
Both ignored Rust selectors and `HC074_PARENT_COHORT` are manual non-ship gates.

Use only an independently approved isolated environment without overlapping
builds/tests. The prototype phase requires its exact frozen baseline image.
Keep first failures without retry-to-pass. The first integrated full preparation
still expires; its separate residual profile is attribution only, not a new
functional verdict or evidence of full-preparation speedup.
